      "player": "Haiku Coach",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "**OH NO!** Opponent just cast **Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury** on the stack! It has:\n\
- **When it enters, it deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life**\n\
- **Escape** ability\n\
\n\
And there's a note: \"When {this} enters or attacks, it deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.\"\n\
\n\
This means when Phlage enters the battlefield, it will deal 3 damage - exactly my current life total! **I'm about to lose!**\n\
\n\
Opponent has 1 red mana in pool. They can target me with that 3 damage and:\n\
- Deal 3 damage to me (reducing me from 13 to 10)\n\
- Wait, that's not lethal...\n\
\n\
Actually let me reread. Phlage \"deals 3 damage to **any target**\". That could be me, a creature, or itself. And Phlage entered - so when it ETB, it triggers and deals 3 damage.\n\
\n\
But wait - that only brings me to 10 life. Not lethal. Unless they have something else...\n\
\n\
Let me see what's in the stack and what's happening. The game says Phlage is on the stack still. Let me wait for the resolve:",
