    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Johnny has Stubborn Denial in hand and Arid Mesa on the battlefield with Leyline of the Guildpact (making Arid Mesa every basic land type, so it can tap for any color including blue). Stubborn Denial costs {U} and would counter Thoughtseize (a noncreature spell) unless the opponent pays {1}. The opponent has only a Swamp and Urza's Saga (which on chapter I can only add {C}), and already spent {B} to cast Thoughtseize, so they have no mana available to pay the {1}. This would be a hard counter effectively. Instead, Johnny declined to respond and let Thoughtseize resolve, which will strip one of their important cards (likely Territorial Kavu or Leyline Binding). Countering Thoughtseize with Stubborn Denial would be a clean 1-for-1 trade protecting their entire hand.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to respond to Thoughtseize, allowing it to resolve and letting the opponent strip a card from hand.",
      "better_line": "Tap Arid Mesa for {U} (enabled by Leyline of the Guildpact) and cast Stubborn Denial targeting Thoughtseize. The opponent has no mana to pay {1}, so it would be countered.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 15,
      "player": "Gem3F Johnny",
      "decision_index": 29,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Phlage is a strong card but it requires escape cost (RRWW + exile 5 cards from graveyard), meaning it won't come back easily. Meanwhile, Leyline Binding with Leyline of the Guildpact on the battlefield costs only W (since all lands are every basic type, giving 5 domain), and it can exile any nonland permanent including Urza's Saga or Nethergoyf. Leyline Binding is essentially a 1-mana removal spell that could answer any threat Haiku Coach deploys. Stubborn Denial is also worth considering since with a 4+ power creature (Territorial Kavu with domain or Nethergoyf), it becomes a hard counter that could protect key permanents or counter Kozilek's Command.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Phlage, Titan of Fire's Fury with Thoughtseize",
      "better_line": "Discard Leyline Binding, which is effectively a 1-mana exile effect thanks to Leyline of the Guildpact's domain bonus and threatens to answer any permanent Haiku Coach plays including Urza's Saga constructs and Nethergoyf. Phlage requires significant resources to escape and the opponent only has 1 card in graveyard.",
