    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Leyline of the Guildpact on the battlefield, all lands are every basic land type, making Leyline Binding cost just {W} (5 less due to domain). The player has an untapped Arid Mesa that could tap for mana (since it's every basic land type thanks to Leyline of the Guildpact). However, the opponent has no nonland permanents worth exiling right now (Urza's Saga is a land). More importantly, the player should be deploying Territorial Kavu this turn as a 5/5 threat (all 5 basic land types), but they have only 1 land untapped and no Mountain in play yet. They should activate Arid Mesa to fetch a Mountain, then cast Territorial Kavu. By passing without activating Arid Mesa or playing their Mountain from hand, they miss deploying a 5/5 on turn 2.",
