    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Leyline of the Guildpact on the battlefield, all lands are every basic land type, meaning Leyline Binding costs only {W} (5 less due to domain). The player could also activate Arid Mesa to fetch a Mountain (or any land), thinning the deck and enabling revolt for future Fatal Pushes. More importantly, passing without cracking Arid Mesa means missing the opportunity to use that mana efficiently. The player has Territorial Kavu to cast next turn (which would be a 5/5 with Leyline of the Guildpact), but declining to crack Arid Mesa at end of opponent's turn is a small missed optimization - they could crack it now to have two untapped lands next turn while keeping options open.",
