    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing Territorial Kavu before combat is generally fine since there's no combat yet on turn 2 going first, but the player should consider whether playing Mountain first (to ensure the land drop) and then Kavu would be better sequencing. More importantly, playing Kavu before playing the Mountain means if they want to hold up Stubborn Denial after playing Mountain, they'd have exactly the mana. However, the real concern is sequencing: playing a creature before combat when holding Stubborn Denial (a trick) isn't relevant here since it's their own turn. The bigger question is whether to play Mountain first before committing the Kavu - if Kavu resolves, they can play Mountain and hold up Stubborn Denial with Ferocious active (Kavu is 5/5 with Leyline making all lands every basic type). Actually, the order doesn't matter much since the opponent is tapped out. This play seems reasonable.",
