    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Haiku Coach declined to cast Fatal Push on Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer during their own precombat main phase. Ragavan is a high-value threat that generates card advantage and Treasure tokens every time it connects. Fatal Push can destroy it (mana value 1, well within the 2-or-less threshold). While waiting until the opponent's combat to cast it is sometimes correct, there's no downside to killing Ragavan now since it's already on the battlefield and the opponent has tapped-out lands. Additionally, Haiku Coach has Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth making all lands Swamps, so they have plenty of black mana available. The 'reasoning' suggests they thought it was the opponent's turn, but it's actually Haiku Coach's own precombat main - this appears to be a misread of the game state. However, Ragavan could also be attacked into with Nethergoyf, so killing it with Push while it could be dealt with in combat is a minor resource waste. The real issue is passing without doing anything when they could have removed a dangerous threat.",
