      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Haiku Coach has Fatal Push in hand and Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer (a 2/1 for mana value 1) on the opponent's battlefield. Ragavan is one of the most dangerous creatures in Modern - every time it connects it generates a Treasure token and exiles a card from the opponent's library that can be cast. Fatal Push cleanly kills it (mana value 1, well under the 2 threshold). There's no reason to hold Fatal Push here when it can be cast at instant speed on the opponent's end step or right now during post-combat main. By passing without casting it, Haiku Coach gives the opponent another turn to attack with Ragavan and generate value. Additionally, all of the opponent's lands are tapped, so there's no risk of a counterspell (Stubborn Denial was revealed earlier in the game).",
