      "description": "At 6 life facing a tapped Nethergoyf (which will untap and attack next turn for 5+ damage), Gem3F Johnny declined to cast Lightning Bolt. While the Nethergoyf is tapped and can't be killed by Bolt alone (it's likely a 5/6 given 8 card types in graveyard), using Bolt to go to the face (opponent at 13) doesn't accomplish much either. However, the player could cast Lightning Bolt targeting the opponent to get closer to a burn kill, especially since they're in a racing situation at 6 life. The decision to hold Bolt is defensible if they're planning to use it reactively, but with Consign to Memory for interaction and being so low on life, getting damage in while they can is worth considering.",
