      "description": "Haiku Coach has Inquisition of Kozilek in hand and enough mana to cast it (Urborg makes all lands Swamps, so any untapped land produces black). The opponent Gem3F Johnny has no cards in hand currently visible, but Inquisition forces a reveal which provides information. However, looking more carefully at the board state, most lands are tapped except Urborg, Tomb of Yawgmoth and the two Eldrazi Spawn tokens. Urborg can tap for {B} to cast Inquisition. Even if the opponent has no cards in hand (the board state doesn't explicitly show Johnny's hand size), casting Inquisition is free information at worst. But the reasoning says 'Johnny is out of cards' - if that's truly the case, Inquisition would fizzle with no nonland cards to choose. The real missed opportunity is that Shadowspear could be equipped to an Eldrazi Spawn token for 2 mana (using Eldrazi Temple which is tapped, so this isn't possible either). Actually, looking at the tapped lands more carefully - Swamp tapped, Ifnir Deadlands tapped, Eldrazi Temple tapped, Prismatic Vista tapped. Only Urborg is untapped. So Haiku Coach has only 1 mana available ({B} from Urborg) plus potentially sacrificing Spawn tokens for {C} each. They could cast Inquisition with that 1 {B} from Urborg. If Johnny truly has 0 cards, it's a wasted spell. But the decision was to pass entirely rather than even attempting Inquisition, which at minimum provides hand information confirmation. This is a very minor issue.",
